the universe; the top four hold 25% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted higher, up 15% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 17% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 21% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 54% and a beta of 0.87, it moves roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 1.78 vs 5y 0.80), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $219.6M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 29% in the 2020 crash, 43% in the 2022 bear market and 87% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $19.92 (margin of safety -558%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 22%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Basic Materials peers: P/E 28.5 vs 15.4 and EV/EBITDA 20.8 vs 7.9 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 10% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an EBIT/EV of 2.6% (vs the 8% bar).","The 10 covering analysts target $170 on average, 29% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 8% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.9%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.69).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.29x.","ROE of 17% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.1x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 26pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 83.7, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 7.78)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 29.5% over 3 years and 16.1% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 28%).